    <statement><p>Are the following statements true or false?</p>
<p><ol>
<li>
<p>The value of <m>\vec{v} \cdot (\vec{v} \times \vec{w})</m> is always zero.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>If <m>\vec{v}</m> and <m>\vec{w}</m> are any two vectors, then <m>||\vec{v} + \vec{w}|| = ||\vec{v}|| + ||\vec{w}||</m>.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>For any scalar <m>c</m> and any vector <m>\vec{v}</m>, we have <m>||c\vec{v}|| = c ||\vec{v}||</m>.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>(\vec{i} \times \vec{j}) \cdot \vec{k} = \vec{i} \cdot (\vec{j} \times \vec{k})</m>.</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</statement>
